{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts","id":641688,"title":"Power Level of Beasts??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-27T09:03:20-07:00","id":641688,"title":"Power Level of Beasts??","content":"Now maybe it's a little shallow for me to be thinking about this, but how do Beasts stack up to the other species in combat? It seems to me that they would be absolutely owned by an uratha, kindred, Promethean, demon, and so on hands-down. Now you can metagame and just go for the most powerful lair traits you can get in order to cause massive aggravated or lethal damage in the area,but that can also harm you as well at low lair level. I'm not saying that they should just become all-out tanks that destroy everything, but they seem to be rather squishy. Minus a specific atavism, beasts can only use satiety to heal when in their lair. <br /> <br /> Against a vampire, any attacks that cause lethal are reduced to bashing, the vampire can heal using vitae, and its disciplines would surely mess up the beast. <br /> <br /> An uratha is a regen god and with its combat forms it also deals crazy damage. Add gifts into the mix and the beast will be cut apart within a matter of turns.<br /> <br /> There is one family, however, Eshmaki, that seem to just be significantly better than the other families combat-wise. Limb-from-limb allows them to do lethal damage relative to their lair level and they can cause aggravated damage at the expenditure of satiety. They can use dragon's breathe, which is a vampire's nightmare and can also cause aggravated damage. They get the relentless-hunter atavism, allowing them some heal capabilities. Then there is From-The-Shadows, which gives a huge chance to provide a surprise attack which can then be coupled with limb-from-limb or dragon's breathe to do aggravated damage. <br /> <br /> Now I'm not butt hurt over this, but i would like to see other people's opinions on this. Perhaps I'm looking at this wrong, or maybe I've missed a lot and am just an idiot lol. But either way, it seems Eshmaki are above the other families and beasts are below the other supernaturals when they should be able to really hold their own, as they are most definitely made for cross-over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T10:49:18-07:00","id":641813,"title":"","content":"I'm working off of the older draft so I don't know if any of this has changed, but I think Beasts would tend to be more like Mages in combat. If you give a Beast time to prepare and set up the environment in the right way to invoke her Lair Traits, you can usually kiss your ass goodbye. Some of the Major Lair Traits can get really, really nasty, as in &quot;Lock you down so you can't move, put you in pitch blackness so you can't see, and burn you with Aggravated acid damage each round.&quot; And the Beast is immune to all of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T11:50:45-07:00","id":641909,"title":"","content":"That's true enough and I can get behind that. I think it would still be nice to have a faster heal option that doesn't require the beast to be in its lair, as a typical street thug could put a beast down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T12:26:44-07:00","id":641935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tylerjohnny1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=641909#post641909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true enough and I can get behind that. I think it would still be nice to have a faster heal option that doesn't require the beast to be in its lair, as a typical street thug could put a beast down.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps you could write up a Merit that lets them spend Satiety outside their Lair. Said Merit would probably be worth 3 or more dots, possibly with a prerequisite of Lair 3 or 4. <br /> <br /> You could have another Merit that lets them hold more than 10 points of Satiety. This Merit might have a Lair 3 or 4 prerequisite, and require them to spend 1 willpower point and/or roll Stamina + Resolve every so often to avoid going dormant, thus becoming more vulnerable against Heroes and other enemies. You could hold 2 extra Satiety per dot in the Merit, up to a maximum of 10 extra Satiety. The amount of extra Satiety you are holding might impose a penalty to your Stamina + Resolve roll, like how humans feel sleepy after a big meal. Every 2 extra Satiety (round down) imposes a -1 penalty. I'd call this Merit &quot;Smorgasbord&quot;.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-27-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T12:31:14-07:00","id":641938,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's as true as you think. A prospective Beast has to pay at least a cursory attention to combat in order to be effective, but they have a lot of options that fit into a wide variety of situations. What hypthetical thug are you concerned will harm a starting beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T12:45:34-07:00","id":641953,"title":"","content":"I think it depends since in theory you're picking atavisms based on what your Beast is as opposed to cherry picking so your troll can breath fire.* Also the question is are we bringing Nightmares into this equation? Cause I think hitting a werewolf with &quot;All your Teeth Fall Out&quot; is going to tip the scales in combat a little.<br /> But assuming your fighting a Beast that is only using the inherent abilities and atavisms of its family there are some details to consider. Of course this is looking at very specific Beasts and not ones based of custom nightmares like the Horror in the All Knowing Website thread, and assuming one that has no overlap with other families even though that is open rather easily. I mean Dragons easily fit into three of five families and I believe in one thread we discussed making a Heckatonkire a Makara just as easily as we could make it an Anakim.<br /> <br /> The Ugallu tend to be flyers, so anyone wanting to pick a fight with one of them has to deal with the fact that the opponent is going to be fighting you from outside of your combat range and Eye of Heaven means they will be able to pick up on any weaknesses you have. Whether or not said weakness is exploitable is of course up for debate, but it is worth noting. Also if its willing to throw satiety into the equation they can create a hurricane or a lightning storm.<br /> <br /> The Makara are probably not the most combat oriented as far as atavisms go. Though they will probably be fighting in favorable terrain if they can help it,so if you let one pick the terrain your odds of wining the fight will be influenced by how well you can fight in 30 feet of water.<br /> <br /> The Anakim are raw force. Meaning the biggest stuff in the terrain will come flying at you or be used to smash your skull and they can probably hit like a truck anyway.<br /> <br /> You've already listed that the Eshmaki can mess people up in straight up fight.<br /> <br /> Namtaru can have a contact poison, so that's a variable trait there as it depends on how susceptible to poison the target is.Shadowed Soul allows for a Beast to cease being physical in the dark and a nice teleport to make it harder to keep a bead on them. Unbreakable can put one of these guys on a level of resilience that is just a pain to hit through. Finally Infestation means that a Beast can just turn into a swarm and use that to rip at an enemy.<br /> <br /> Of course these would be a Beast fighting at its weakest since as previously mentioned we're going with the idea of a Beast who only knows its favored atavisms, so no gryphon with razor sharp claws, no kraken with the strength to crush a ship in its tentacles, and no rock monster that just has bullets plink off of it; not using lair traits which Brian88 mentioned can seriously tilt a fight in the Beasts favor; no weaponry outside of stuff already in the enviorment so no Ugallu shooting at the vampire from the sky; and no Nightmares to cover other weaknesses even if none are as obscenely dangerous as &quot;You are Meat&quot; was.<br /> <br /> *Not that such a thing is wrong. So help me god if you can't inspire nightmares with the power to use a truck as a projectile punch through walls and breath fire you aren't trying hard enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:11:55-07:00","id":642000,"title":"","content":"Just skimmed Beast's powers. They are rather extremely offensive in nature. A beast with almost any of the offensive Atavisms or more powerful Nightmares is at <i>least</i> as deadly to other characters as they are to him, even without innate defensive powers. A beast can also take Unbreakable, Relentless Hunter, Infested, and/or (Advanced/Epic) Iron Skin to shore up their defenses quite nicely.<br /> <br /> In terms of matching theme, keep in mind that in a proper brood a Beast can select Atavisms, etc. that are keyed to other people in the Brood's themes as well as your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-27-2015, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:16:59-07:00","id":642007,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input from all of you, you've helped me see it from a different angle. The problem is probably just that I come from requiem and a LOT of forsaken, so I put the beast in situations where the upfront werewolf would be at its prime. So said street thug situation was close-quarters hand-to-hand, which actually came from anecdote in the book where two werewolves had to bail out a beast who was being beaten to a pulp by a thug with a crowbar. <br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the biggest reason for my concern was, as stated above, coming into beast with a forsaken mentality. I'm used to being able to be gutted and then use essence to patch it back up. I also only really glanced at the mechanical value of nightmares, so big mistake there on my end.<br /> <br /> Off-topic question: How does a beast aquire atavisms from a different family? Is it from kinship with another beast? And if so, does that kinship give the beast all of that family's atavisms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:27:15-07:00","id":642019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=641953#post641953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it depends since in theory you're picking atavisms based on what your Beast is as opposed to cherry picking so your troll can breath fire.* Also the question is are we bringing Nightmares into this equation? Cause I think hitting a werewolf with &quot;All your Teeth Fall Out&quot; is going to tip the scales in combat a little.<br /> But assuming your fighting a Beast that is only using the inherent abilities and atavisms of its family there are some details to consider. Of course this is looking at very specific Beasts and not ones based of custom nightmares like the Horror in the All Knowing Website thread, and assuming one that has no overlap with other families even though that is open rather easily. I mean Dragons easily fit into three of five families and I believe in one thread we discussed making a Heckatonkire a Makara just as easily as we could make it an Anakim.<br /> <br /> The Ugallu tend to be flyers, so anyone wanting to pick a fight with one of them has to deal with the fact that the opponent is going to be fighting you from outside of your combat range and Eye of Heaven means they will be able to pick up on any weaknesses you have. Whether or not said weakness is exploitable is of course up for debate, but it is worth noting. Also if its willing to throw satiety into the equation they can create a hurricane or a lightning storm.<br /> <br /> The Makara are probably not the most combat oriented as far as atavisms go. Though they will probably be fighting in favorable terrain if they can help it,so if you let one pick the terrain your odds of wining the fight will be influenced by how well you can fight in 30 feet of water.<br /> <br /> The Anakim are raw force. Meaning the biggest stuff in the terrain will come flying at you or be used to smash your skull and they can probably hit like a truck anyway.<br /> <br /> You've already listed that the Eshmaki can mess people up in straight up fight.<br /> <br /> Namtaru can have a contact poison, so that's a variable trait there as it depends on how susceptible to poison the target is.Shadowed Soul allows for a Beast to cease being physical in the dark and a nice teleport to make it harder to keep a bead on them. Unbreakable can put one of these guys on a level of resilience that is just a pain to hit through. Finally Infestation means that a Beast can just turn into a swarm and use that to rip at an enemy.<br /> <br /> Of course these would be a Beast fighting at its weakest since as previously mentioned we're going with the idea of a Beast who only knows its favored atavisms, so no gryphon with razor sharp claws, no kraken with the strength to crush a ship in its tentacles, and no rock monster that just has bullets plink off of it; not using lair traits which Brian88 mentioned can seriously tilt a fight in the Beasts favor; no weaponry outside of stuff already in the enviorment so no Ugallu shooting at the vampire from the sky; and no Nightmares to cover other weaknesses even if none are as obscenely dangerous as &quot;You are Meat&quot; was.<br /> <br /> *Not that such a thing is wrong. So help me god if you can't inspire nightmares with the power to use a truck as a projectile punch through walls and breath fire you aren't trying hard enough.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had thought of Beasts using normal terrain and Lair Traits for combat before, but you went more in depth and I liked it. You get a Like. I don't know much about the crunch of Beast, though.<br /> <br /> I considered writing up a Fighting Style that lets you mix and match features of your Atavisms and Lair Traits into each attack. Said Fighting Style should work in the Astral as well, methinks. Each maneuver, besides requiring the previous one, might have certain Atavisms and/or Lair Traits as prerequisites. I am not exactly sure how that would work, but I could take cues from the Fighting Styles of other monsters in 2ed, like Kindred Dueling for vampires and Relentless Assault + Tactical Shifting for werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-27-2015, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:30:05-07:00","id":642023,"title":"","content":"It partially depends on the Beast. Atavisms aren't powers in the normal sense, they are functions of the body. For example think your standard werewolf in its chrinos state. You've got claws and sharp teeth, these aren't special powers the werewolf has or needs to learn its just part of their nature, In the same way a Beast can have atavisms outside of its family because they are just part of the Beast's nature. For example an Ugallu gryphon possessing rending claws because well gryphons have claws. As a result they tend to just be things you have as opposed to things you learn and you do need to come up with more of a reason for some atavisms to be acquired later than others might. Ie not hard to justify an Eshamaki dragon eventually learning Needs Must to hunt things for their hoard, bit trickier to justify that same dragon suddenly becoming a swarm of countless tiny lizards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:41:13-07:00","id":642032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642023#post642023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It partially depends on the Beast. Atavisms aren't powers in the normal sense, they are functions of the body. For example think your standard werewolf in its chrinos state. You've got claws and sharp teeth, these aren't special powers the werewolf has or needs to learn its just part of their nature, In the same way a Beast can have atavisms outside of its family because they are just part of the Beast's nature. For example an Ugallu gryphon possessing rending claws because well gryphons have claws. As a result they tend to just be things you have as opposed to things you learn and you do need to come up with more of a reason for some atavisms to be acquired later than others might. Ie not hard to justify an Eshamaki dragon eventually learning Needs Must to hunt things for their hoard, bit trickier to justify that same dragon suddenly becoming a swarm of countless tiny lizards.</div> </div> </div> </div> That does make more sense. I guess the prerequisites would be more sensible as Lair 3, Strength 3, Stamina 3 and Brawl/Weaponry 3. If a maneuver focuses on a improving a Brawl attack, the description might say something like &quot;the Beast attacks with cyclopean fists, spear-tipped tendrils, invisible fangs, skin-flaying wings, corrosive tongues etc&quot;. No Atavisms or Lair Traits would be required. Using individual Lair Traits in a more focused and precise way might be covered by another Merit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:46:52-07:00","id":642038,"title":"","content":"Regulars should know this was coming, so. here's where Beasts fit on the power scale:<br /> <br /> Players who know how to get the most out of their characters and are clever with what they have.<br /> Players who do not.<br /> <br /> THey fit in with both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:48:43-07:00","id":642039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642023#post642023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It partially depends on the Beast. Atavisms aren't powers in the normal sense, they are functions of the body. For example think your standard werewolf in its chrinos state. You've got claws and sharp teeth, these aren't special powers the werewolf has or needs to learn its just part of their nature, In the same way a Beast can have atavisms outside of its family because they are just part of the Beast's nature. For example an Ugallu gryphon possessing rending claws because well gryphons have claws. As a result they tend to just be things you have as opposed to things you learn and you do need to come up with more of a reason for some atavisms to be acquired later than others might. Ie not hard to justify an Eshamaki dragon eventually learning Needs Must to hunt things for their hoard, bit trickier to justify that same dragon suddenly becoming a swarm of countless tiny lizards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I think I misunderstand the character creation then. When you are making your beast, how do you choose your atavisms? How many can you have and what are the restrictions of you're able to overlap families?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:52:59-07:00","id":642042,"title":"","content":"You have to pick one from your family. The other one can be whatever you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T14:34:28-07:00","id":642096,"title":"","content":"There aren't really any restrictions on what atavisms you can pick ,aside from the restriction Elfive mentioned for character gen, it just comes down to the concept of what kind of creature your Beast's inner Horror is. The Worm that Walks is obvious for Beast with the infestation atavism, Smaug is significantly less so though he is practically iconic for one with dragonfire because well dragon. To that end learning new atavisms fit in with your concept can be justified in a number of ways like an anakim tyrant brawler taking unbreakable and saying &quot;Well I've been in a lot of fights and my Horror has matured, so I'm far more durable than I used to be.&quot; So there isn't a restriction preventing you from being a being formed of countless fire ants who can also use dragonfire because you're made of <i>fire ants</i> beyond that your ST might veto it as not fitting concept. To that end some atavisms are more likely to crop up in extended play than others, as I imagine Needs Must would require work to create a concept that <b>can't </b> justify getting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:14:02-07:00","id":642131,"title":"","content":"Beasts are interesting in that they have a lot of potent offensive options but relatively little defensively. The one thing they do have, though, is the Unbreakable Atavism. It gives a minimum 3/2 armor, which is quite a lot considering how easy it is to get. I don't know about werewolves, but vampires have to spend a good deal more to get that kind of armor, as do most changelings besides Metalflesh (who are absurdly tanky in 2e)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:51:35-07:00","id":642159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642131#post642131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are interesting in that they have a lot of potent offensive options but relatively little defensively. The one thing they do have, though, is the Unbreakable Atavism. It gives a minimum 3/2 armor, which is quite a lot considering how easy it is to get. I don't know about werewolves, but vampires have to spend a good deal more to get that kind of armor, as do most changelings besides Metalflesh (who are absurdly tanky in 2e)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good point, it seems that so long as they are the hunter they are good, but they are very vulnerable when they don't have it set up their way. I suppose that could be held true for all splats though. <br /> <br /> I guess only through playing will we see how they do in the world, and the final version of the book may be drastically different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:58:34-07:00","id":642163,"title":"","content":"There's too much open to debate. A Beast is more XP efficent than other supernaturals - they only need to raise Lair and the occasional Atavism instead of both Potency and a Discipline/Renown/Arcana track. That said, that's white room theorycrafting, and lots of Beats also get contacts/allies/mentors/retainers/etc in the various supernatural communities, and some want Nightmares, etc. There's a lot going on here.<br /> <br /> When it comes down to comparing splats, you have to realize each has their own specialties. Vampires excell at controls - self, grappling, mind f@#$-ery, subordinants. Werewolves are hunters, shapeshifters, and pack people. Mages are researchers, investigators, and shielding experts. Changelings are dreamers and illusionists. Demons are spies and religious figures. When it comes to the speciality, that particular supernatural tends to excell beyond others. So, if we did a competition for getting someone to give them a free drink, vampires generally win - blood bonds and mind control tends to beat out everyone else who still needs to use Social Maneuvers. Werewolves can track people they never met by where their shadow passed. That's stuff that's very hard, if impossible, for others to mimic.<br /> <br /> No one has a specialty of &quot;combat master.&quot; When it comes to combat, everyone is close enough that luck, environment, and specific builds play too large of a part to make it definite call. A vampire against a demon? Well, the demon will generally win... if it has fire powers to use in combat. A Messanger (without any fire) against a Daeva? The daeva could generally take the demon. There are few who can keep up with a fully armored mage in terms of defense, but a power like Dominate, The Look, or some Dominance Gifts cut through it like butter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T16:01:14-07:00","id":642166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642096#post642096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Smaug is significantly less so though he is practically iconic for one with dragonfire because well dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not picking on you specififcally, Nalak, but just saying this:<br /> <br /> Dragons can fit into any Family and any Hunger, and with any Atavism. Beast: the Primordial could very well have been Dragon: the Primordial, everything matches so well, but there's zero reason to restrict the game to flying lizards. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T16:04:23-07:00","id":642168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642131#post642131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are interesting in that they have a lot of potent offensive options but relatively little defensively. The one thing they do have, though, is the Unbreakable Atavism. It gives a minimum 3/2 armor, which is quite a lot considering how easy it is to get. I don't know about werewolves, but vampires have to spend a good deal more to get that kind of armor, as do most changelings besides Metalflesh (who are absurdly tanky in 2e)</div> </div> </div> </div> They have the Unbreakable Atavism, they have Lair Traits that grant immunity to tilts, they have the Atavism that heals them, and there's the flying Atavism that lets them fly really fast, and evade being hit by anyone (can't hit wha'ts out of your reach!) The Infestation Atavism turns you into a swarm that's shrugging off damage, since you're a swarm. <br /> <br /> There are plenty of defensive options, though none of them directly boost Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T16:08:23-07:00","id":642172,"title":"","content":"There's also one that gives them extra health, don't forget that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T16:14:07-07:00","id":642176,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes, the Giant Size Atavism. I keep forgetting about the extra health, mostly because I drool over the intimidation factor it comes with. I love my social powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T16:27:09-07:00","id":642182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642166#post642166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not picking on you specififcally, Nalak, but just saying this:<br /> <br /> Dragons can fit into any Family and any Hunger, and with any Atavism. Beast: the Primordial could very well have been Dragon: the Primordial, everything matches so well, but there's zero reason to restrict the game to flying lizards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh my point was more that its harder to justify a Beast gaining some atavisms than it is others depending on what your theme is. I used dragons because they're a fairly standard one that while there are a few different versions a person can have in mind there are enough details that I would be more surprised to find a person couldn't instantly think of a dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T17:31:35-07:00","id":642208,"title":"","content":"Ok, how about something a bit more concrete? Can you guys build various different combat specialists with Beast? The caveat here is that this doesn't conclusively <i>prove</i> anything, it just serves as an exercise in theorycraft.<br /> <br /> So how about it? Using Beast, how would you build the best ... striking brawler? Grappler? Melee weaponsmaster? Avoidance defender? Endurance defender? Gun-fu expert?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T17:36:04-07:00","id":642229,"title":"","content":"Over 9000!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T18:29:21-07:00","id":642305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642208#post642208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, how about something a bit more concrete? Can you guys build various different combat specialists with Beast? The caveat here is that this doesn't conclusively <i>prove</i> anything, it just serves as an exercise in theorycraft.</div> </div> </div> </div> Like... what kind of combat specialists? I mean, they're pretty basic. Most options are going to revolve around being stealth + poison, an elementalist, super strength tank, fly-by-shooting, Infestation-swarming, and a Nightmare-mystic. Most likely, a combination of two or more of the Atavisms, since other beasts have immunities from lair or the same powers (ie two beasts with Dragonfire can't hurt each other). That's really a thing with the Begotten - immuities.<br /> <br /> <br /> My money is on anyone with Infestation. Its impossible to take on a swarm without some kind of area-attack or psychic ability, usually some kind of attack. Its easy to get the appropriate fire and storm resistances (the big two), some speed bumps to keep up with anyone, and attack them. Its cheap and effective - the only defense is having armor that covers your entire body AND negates all the damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T19:30:08-07:00","id":642363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642305#post642305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like... what kind of combat specialists? I mean, they're pretty basic. Most options are going to revolve around being stealth + poison, an elementalist, super strength tank, fly-by-shooting, Infestation-swarming, and a Nightmare-mystic. Most likely, a combination of two or more of the Atavisms, since other beasts have immunities from lair or the same powers (ie two beasts with Dragonfire can't hurt each other). That's really a thing with the Begotten - immuities.<br /> <br /> <br /> My money is on anyone with Infestation. Its impossible to take on a swarm without some kind of area-attack or psychic ability, usually some kind of attack. Its easy to get the appropriate fire and storm resistances (the big two), some speed bumps to keep up with anyone, and attack them. Its cheap and effective - the only defense is having armor that covers your entire body AND negates all the damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa, hold on a minute. I don't remember atavisms giving you immunities to that power, such as dragonfire as you say. In fact, I don't even knowing lair traits give you complete immunities to everything. Like having a poisonous lair, does that make you immune to the basilisk venom atavism? The flame trait in a lair gives you immunity to fire based off of your lair rating, but the electrifying trait gives immunity up to whatever damage the lair does, which why wouldn't you choose the most damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T20:00:17-07:00","id":642394,"title":"","content":"You are immune to environmental tilts that are shared by your lair traits. This doesn't normally extend to the entire element. To go with the whole fire thing if you have burning (I think there were levels to it, but we'll ignore it for simplicity) as a lair trait then you could walk into a burning building and ignore the enviormental tilt it imposes because your Beast lives in that kind of thing. I would argue that if you're in your lair that it might upgrade as you'll be fully your Beast self there as opposed to a human with the Horror bleeding through. Ie if your Horror is Cthuga* you can walk through a burning building without too much of a problem because the ambient bleed out from Horror would protect you. A flamethrower would probably still burn you though. In your lair though I might argue fire immunity on the grounds that you become a being of fire and thus normal flames have no more effect on you.**<br /> <br /> *Elder God of living fire. The version I think of looks like a giant angry flaming tiger<br /> **Seriously not backed by anything, but its my two cents.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T03:22:44-07:00","id":642801,"title":"","content":"Healing a point of lethal every 30 minutes is completely irrelevant in a combat scenario that will be over in 30 seconds. One bashing per round can help, but only if you have enough armor that enemy attacks are getting reduced to just one bashing. Infestation reduces some types of lethal to bashing at low satiety and allows you to punish melee attackers at the cost of some of your own health but you can still be hurt by bludgeoning weapons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T04:07:26-07:00","id":642826,"title":"","content":"I feel that a Beast that doesn't not initiate the combat nor switch to its Lair when facing a serious threat is crippling itself, so under those circumstances I don't really care if they would get stomped by everything else. The Lair <i>is</i> a Beast's greatest defensive asset. Going to battle and leaving your armor at home is unwise to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T05:29:43-07:00","id":642868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tylerjohnny1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642363#post642363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa, hold on a minute. I don't remember atavisms giving you immunities to that power, such as dragonfire as you say.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going off the preview document, but under Dragonfire it says, &quot;Furthermore, fire causes no damage to the Beast, and she never suffers environmental penalties or damage caused by heat and smoke, which are like clear air to her. This is in addition to any environmental immunity from Lair Traits (see p. XX).&quot; <br /> <br /> As well, under Shadowed Soul, it says, &quot;Darkness is not only the Beast\u2019s natural state, it is her ally and does not impede her in any way. She can \u201csee\u201d in total darkness, including that created by supernatural powers, as if it were broad daylight. Furthermore, she is immune to the Blinded Tilt regardless of its cause.&quot; <br /> <br /> Relentless Assult provides immunity to being stunned or incompacitated, and a huge bonus to resisting any poison damage.<br /> <br /> Immunities to Tilts and the like is a pretty big Beast advantage. Yes, the Lair only protects against Environmental Tilts. But when you're a swarm of bugs, there's only a limited number of non-environmental tilts that can affect you. Poison isn't an out-and-out immunity, but it is highly resistable. <br /> <br /> Now, if that changed for the final version, then I stand corrected. But, going by what I have now, its a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T05:53:45-07:00","id":642885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642305#post642305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like... what kind of combat specialists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like... The kinds I pointed out at the end of my post?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T06:53:27-07:00","id":642922,"title":"","content":"Working off an older version of the text, let's take a look at the Lair Trait example of Crushing. It's a Major Trait, but any halfway-savvy player shouldn't have much trouble invoking it. The Trait is a Level 4 Extreme Environment, and &quot;some&quot; forms &quot;may&quot; allow rolls to break free. That's almost game-over right there all by itself, especially if the GM doesn't allow rolls to break free of the effects. The environment just starts squeezing people until they pop, and there's nothing they can do about it, not even move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T08:33:38-07:00","id":643023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642208#post642208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, how about something a bit more concrete? Can you guys build various different combat specialists with Beast? The caveat here is that this doesn't conclusively <i>prove</i> anything, it just serves as an exercise in theorycraft.<br /> <br /> So how about it? Using Beast, how would you build the best ... striking brawler? Grappler? Melee weaponsmaster? Avoidance defender? Endurance defender? Gun-fu expert?</div> </div> </div> </div>For something like that you'd have to set a couple of parameters like...Experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T08:33:41-07:00","id":643024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642868#post642868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm going off the preview document, but under Dragonfire it says, &quot;Furthermore, fire causes no damage to the Beast, and she never suffers environmental penalties or damage caused by heat and smoke, which are like clear air to her. This is in addition to any environmental immunity from Lair Traits (see p. XX).&quot;<br /> <br /> As well, under Shadowed Soul, it says, &quot;Darkness is not only the Beast\u2019s natural state, it is her ally and does not impede her in any way. She can \u201csee\u201d in total darkness, including that created by supernatural powers, as if it were broad daylight. Furthermore, she is immune to the Blinded Tilt regardless of its cause.&quot;<br /> <br /> Relentless Assult provides immunity to being stunned or incompacitated, and a huge bonus to resisting any poison damage.<br /> <br /> Immunities to Tilts and the like is a pretty big Beast advantage. Yes, the Lair only protects against Environmental Tilts. But when you're a swarm of bugs, there's only a limited number of non-environmental tilts that can affect you. Poison isn't an out-and-out immunity, but it is highly resistable.<br /> <br /> Now, if that changed for the final version, then I stand corrected. But, going by what I have now, its a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't have any other versions, so no, I was just wrong. I have a hard time memorizing all of these systems without actually playing it, which makes it hard for me to actually know where beasts stand at times.<br /> <br /> Something else that troubles me a little is the roll for using primordial pathways. You take a -2 for low satiety right off the bat, a -3 if the external end of the pathway is in the physical world, and the roll is wits+resolve, not even +lair. Is this roll necessary if you're using the actual physical representation of a chamber? I mean hell, uratha roll int+presence+Primal Urge, normally without any penalties. Also, the roll for using skeleton key uses Resolve+Occult+Lair, a higher pool for going somewhere other than your own lair. Now if you can, without a roll, enter your lair from a chamber you made, then perhaps this isn't so bad. Otherwise, wtf.<br /> <br /> An additional question I have: If a location is resonant with your lair, thereby having one of your environmental traits, there is no cost or roll to impose another one, right? And is it an instant action?<br /> <br /> Edit: I have just now really read through the nightmares, and honestly I feel foolish for not factoring them into combat. If you just look at low-satiety combat, which I did, beasts don't seem to be particularly great or anything, but if you use both ends of the spectrum (starting off high satiety and then burning through to low satiety on nightmares), you can really be a force. This is especially true when a beast is fighting on his own turf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7474,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","user":"Tylerjohnny1","date":". 08-28-2015, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T08:46:39-07:00","id":643032,"title":"","content":"The last version I read had the -3 for places in the material <i>other</i> than the one it was made from. <br /> <br /> Also I'm pretty sure that using skeleton key to open a primodial pathway still goes to your lair. That's the only place it <i>can go. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T09:23:55-07:00","id":643058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643032#post643032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last version I read had the -3 for places in the material <i>other</i> than the one it was made from.<br /> <br /> Also I'm pretty sure that using skeleton key to open a primodial pathway still goes to your lair. That's the only place it <i>can go. </i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But why isn't your lair rating included in the roll when you're using it at a chamber or a similar location, but it is used in skeleton key. And with skeleton key, I was referring to using say a locus to enter the shadow. That roll uses a whole other stat, which I find strange. What I'm really trying to say is that liar should be used to enter your lair from a chamber, it only makes sense, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T09:26:00-07:00","id":643059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=642885#post642885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like... The kinds I pointed out at the end of my post?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's kind of vague. Context would be good. Like I said, immunities are a thing, so its pretty easy to just sit there with two Begotten that stand there and can't hurt the other. Are we fighting other supernaturals, or just building combat capable characters, or...? And, as others have said, simply opening up a powerful Lair Trait can be deadly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tylerjohnny1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643024#post643024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else that troubles me a little is the roll for using primordial pathways. You take a -2 for low satiety right off the bat, a -3 if the external end of the pathway is in the physical world, and the roll is wits+resolve, not even +lair. Is this roll necessary if you're using the actual physical representation of a chamber? I mean hell, uratha roll int+presence+Primal Urge, normally without any penalties. Also, the roll for using skeleton key uses Resolve+Occult+Lair, a higher pool for going somewhere other than your own lair. Now if you can, without a roll, enter your lair from a chamber you made, then perhaps this isn't so bad. Otherwise, wtf.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, its necessary to have the roll, because for someone at High Satiety that gets a +2 bonus, there's a chance at success and calling down the Lair for the duration of the scene instead of a few rounds. As Elfive said, the penalties are slightly different <br /> <br /> Really, there are plenty of ways to enter your Lair if you just want to look around, so the opening of Primordial Pathways is primarily used for pulling your Lair into reality, likely for inflicting Tilts in combat and assuming the Horror form for the extra boost in power. If you have a good Resolve score, not only do you have a good dice pool, but the Pathway stays open for a good amount of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An additional question I have: If a location is resonant with your lair, thereby having one of your environmental traits, there is no cost or roll to impose another one, right? And is it an instant action? </div> </div> </div> Nope, still costs. It just costs more if there's no trait.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: I have just now really read through the nightmares, and honestly I feel foolish for not factoring them into combat. If you just look at low-satiety combat, which I did, beasts don't seem to be particularly great or anything, but if you use both ends of the spectrum (starting off high satiety and then burning through to low satiety on nightmares), you can really be a force. This is especially true when a beast is fighting on his own turf. </div> </div> </div> There's plenty of different ways to run a character. High Satiety Nightmare mystic, Low Satiety Atavistic monster, mix them using Fist of Nightmares and burn Satiety like mad, etc. Can't say which is better, since they all have their benefits and drawbacks.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T11:24:04-07:00","id":643199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643059#post643059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's kind of vague. Context would be good. Like I said, immunities are a thing, so its pretty easy to just sit there with two Begotten that stand there and can't hurt the other. Are we fighting other supernaturals, or just building combat capable characters, or...? And, as others have said, simply opening up a powerful Lair Trait can be deadly.<br /> <br /> Yes, its necessary to have the roll, because for someone at High Satiety that gets a +2 bonus, there's a chance at success and calling down the Lair for the duration of the scene instead of a few rounds. As Elfive said, the penalties are slightly different<br /> <br /> Really, there are plenty of ways to enter your Lair if you just want to look around, so the opening of Primordial Pathways is primarily used for pulling your Lair into reality, likely for inflicting Tilts in combat and assuming the Horror form for the extra boost in power. If you have a good Resolve score, not only do you have a good dice pool, but the Pathway stays open for a good amount of time.<br /> <br /> Nope, still costs. It just costs more if there's no trait.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of different ways to run a character. High Satiety Nightmare mystic, Low Satiety Atavistic monster, mix them using Fist of Nightmares and burn Satiety like mad, etc. Can't say which is better, since they all have their benefits and drawbacks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, just so that I have everything in my head correctly, I'm going to try and go through it and hopefully you'll correct me where/if I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> If a beast is at the location where he created a chamber and wishes to open a primordial pathway, he rolls Wits+Resolve. Being in the mundane world, he suffers a -3. Assuming both lair traits are present, there is then a +2 added. So, in this perfect situation, the roll is Wits+Resolve -1. Fair enough, although I'd still like lair rating to be included.<br /> <br /> Now same situation, but the location is only very similar to where the chamber was created and let's say only one trait is present. You must now spend willpower on the roll since it is not the same exact location. Now, you'll want to add the 2nd trait so that you get that extra +1 die, so you spend a dot of satiety and then roll a separate Wits+Resolve -4(It is only narratively similar, no breaking point occurred here and no exceptional success on a nightmare). Now, you have the 2nd lair trait and complete the roll: Wits+Resolve -1 with a dot of willpower spent.<br /> <br /> Am I correct, or at least close? You say there is a cost to imposing lair traits regardless, but what is the cost of imposing in an area of resonance compared to an area that isn't?<br /> <br /> I appreciate your patience with explaining this, for some reason I'm having a hard time grasping some concepts in this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T12:10:19-07:00","id":643244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tylerjohnny1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643199#post643199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a beast is at the location where he created a chamber and wishes to open a primordial pathway, he rolls Wits+Resolve. Being in the mundane world, he suffers a -3. Assuming both lair traits are present, there is then a +2 added. So, in this perfect situation, the roll is Wits+Resolve -1.</div> </div> </div> </div> No -3 penalty. You actually get a +1 from being in the location you created the chamber instead, +2 from two Tilts being present. So, your roll is Wits+Resolve+3, and you need to spend a point of willpower to make the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now same situation, but the location is only very similar to where the chamber was created and let's say only one trait is present. You must now spend willpower on the roll since it is not the same exact location. Now, you'll want to add the 2nd trait so that you get that extra +1 die, so you spend a dot of satiety and then roll a separate Wits+Resolve -4(It is only narratively similar, no breaking point occurred here and no exceptional success on a nightmare). Now, you have the 2nd lair trait and complete the roll: Wits+Resolve -1 with a dot of willpower spent. </div> </div> </div> First, I don't see any roll for imposing traits. If you have one resonant trait, you can invoke the others with just spending a point of Satity, it seems. Could be mistake, but that's what I'm going with here, according to my document. As for the cost part... &quot;In a location used to create one of her Chambers, a Beast may pay a point of Satiety to impose any of her Lair Traits up to the limit of Traits per scene without needing the initial Tilt. As with opening a Primordial Pathway, Beasts may attempt to use a Chamber in locations that are similar, if not exactly the same, by spending a Willpower point.&quot; Honestly, the rules are a bit mixed up. One section doesn't say an extra cost, another says it does. I'm a bit unclear on cost part the Imposing Trait section, since there seems to be contradicting rules and sections, and there's some debate in the forums over cost. Personally, I say just use one base cost no matter where you are, and let the penalties sort the rest out. Easier to remember that way.<br /> <br /> The current rules don't use &quot;narratively similar,&quot; so its a -3 for being in physical world, and a +2 for Traits imposed, for opening a primordial pathway, for a total of -1 to the Wits+Resolve roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I appreciate your patience with explaining this, for some reason I'm having a hard time grasping some concepts in this book. </div> </div> </div>Well, the rules are confusing, and it seems that they changed between previews, and they may very well be cleaned up more for the final release, making everything here a bit obsolete. So, I wouldn't sweat it too much and just go with what the ST and Players all feel is right until we get an official book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T12:12:42-07:00","id":643246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tylerjohnny1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643199#post643199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Being in the mundane world, he suffers a -3. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. In the place where you made the chamber it's a +1 This is made <i>absolutely explicit </i>in the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T13:55:18-07:00","id":643348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643246#post643246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. In the place where you made the chamber it's a +1 This is made <i>absolutely explicit </i>in the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I don't know what version you have, but the table in mine says only +1 if the external end is in the primordial dream, such as another beasts lair, nothing more. Unless there is another table you're referring to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T13:58:32-07:00","id":643350,"title":"","content":"That's from the latest version. Yours sounds like one of the earlier ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T15:48:25-07:00","id":643511,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B66tiMNn-_PVflpVYlNrQWJXcjRKekdFRmpRdF9ybU5WRzRIc2JmOGdUdUwyaE1SeVBSaFU&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the latest version</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T18:56:45-07:00","id":643686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643059#post643059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's kind of vague. Context would be good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm, I was kind of talking purely mechanically. Dice pools/tricks for the various combat modes, no context needed really. Like how would you put together a Beast geared purely toward being able to punch, kick, or bite really well? How would you put together a grappler? Etc. I don't think that's very vague. Or if it is, it's because it's generic on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T19:41:20-07:00","id":643705,"title":"","content":"After a one-shot cross-over game, I've concluded:<br /> <br /> -Most Major Templates have some form of offensive and defensive innate powers: Vampires are resilient, can heal, and increase their strength, Werewolves regenerate and shapeshift, etc...<br /> Beasts instead of those universal abilities, get Atavisms that are like Demons' Form Abilities (Beasts innate ablities are either not useful in a fight of too situational to be mentioned here).<br /> Except Beasts only get 2 Atavisms at Chargen, while Demons get a truckload of them, although more problematic to access. So, chargen Beasts lag behind most other Supernatural there.<br /> <br /> -Beasts also only get 2 Nightmares, while a Vampire will start with 3 Disciplines, a Demon with 4 Embeds+Exploits, etc...<br /> We had an Eshmaki with Kinship with a Forsaken. She had Relentless Hunter, Needs Must, Behold, my True Form, and Your Tools Betray You. Mimicking some werewolf innate powers cost her her 2 Atavisms, and she was kinda forced to take those 2 Nightmares specifically, because she needed some offensive capability and a Kinship Nightmare, and didn't have the time to make a custom one. It felt a bit like she had to play a werewolf with a single Gift. The player still had lots of fun, though.<br /> <br /> So in short, Beasts start weak but it's nothing that won't be solved by gaining XP.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T22:10:52-07:00","id":643758,"title":"","content":"Skeleton Key is opposed by a supernatural trait so the Beast gets to use Lair. Primordial Pathways is unopposed. I think the reference to willpower in the text is an artifact. It should say &quot;additional&quot; to have any clear meaning. Without that modifier the phrase makes no sense since it always costs willpower. Maybe it can be addressed in the final editing phase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T22:47:24-07:00","id":643798,"title":"","content":"Thank you MCN, having the latest version makes using this forum a lot easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643758#post643758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skeleton Key is opposed by a supernatural trait so the Beast gets to use Lair. Primordial Pathways is unopposed. I think the reference to willpower in the text is an artifact. It should say &quot;additional&quot; to have any clear meaning. Without that modifier the phrase makes no sense since it always costs willpower. Maybe it can be addressed in the final editing phase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point of it being unopposed, but I'm comparing it to an uratha using a locus. Intelligence+Presence+Primal Urge, which uses the supernatural trait in what is also an unopposed roll. Now maybe it's just that stepping through the gauntlet is just different than opening a Primordial Pathway, as the attributes used are indeed very different. That's where I'm coming from at least. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T23:01:08-07:00","id":643804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tylerjohnny1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643798#post643798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point of it being unopposed, but I'm comparing it to an uratha using a locus. Intelligence+Presence+Primal Urge, which uses the supernatural trait in what is also an unopposed roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's 1e. 2e Reaching at a locus is Harmony or 10 - Harmony depending on which way you're jumping as far as werewolves go, and 2e Spirit-Claimed just use Intelligence + Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T23:24:50-07:00","id":643827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=643804#post643804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's 1e. 2e Reaching at a locus is Harmony or 10 - Harmony depending on which way you're jumping as far as werewolves go, and 2e Spirit-Claimed just use Intelligence + Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhhh, I see my mistake. Been using 1e for so long, it's just second nature at this point. I guess old habits die hard then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T15:57:37-07:00","id":644692,"title":"","content":"I would, generally speaking, use the following as the &quot;core&quot; to a combat-oriented Beast build.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b><br /> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 2<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 1, Stamina 5 -OR- Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Horror Attributes</b><br /> Power 2, Finesse 5, Resistance 5 -OR- Power 2, Finesse 5, Resistance 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b><br /> Occult 2, Medicine 1, Athletics 2, Brawl [Grapple] 5, Subterfuge 2, Streetwise 2,<br /> Strongly consider Stealth [Ambushing]<br /> Consider Firearms if you aren't taking Dragonfire<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b><br /> 2 Iron Skin<br /> 2 Iron Skin (Advanced)<br /> 1 Combat Defense [Brawl]<br /> <br /> <i>From here look at:</i><br /> 2 Iron Skin (Epic)<br /> 2 Fist of Nightmares<br /> 3 Killer Instinct + 1 Killer Instinct (Advanced)<br /> 5 Professional Training<br /> 1 Area of Expertise [Grapple]<br /> X More Fighting Styles (Close Quarters Combat, Streetfighting, Relentless Assault, Chokehold,Cheap Shot, and Grappling Style are all solid buys. If you went Strength 1, Dexterity 3 you can get Martial Arts and Defensive Combat Style)<br /> <br /> <i>What and how much depend a lot on how many Merit Dots you are willing to dedicate to Combat, what your spare Atavism is, and whether or not you start with one less chamber in exchange for +2 EXP (it is generally a good idea to do so). Make sure to talk to your ST before taking Professional Training. Rote on combat actions can very quickly get out of hand. On the other hand, there's an atavism to give Rote at the cost of 1 Saity and Willpower is more valuable to Beasts than other Splats so... ymmv.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b><br /> Unbreakable<br /> 1 Other of Choice<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmare:</b><br /> Behold My True Form<br /> 1 Other of Choice<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b><br /> Attributes can be manipulated a little bit. Wits 3, Stamina 4 or 5 and Composure 3 are the important numbers. Strength 2 grants access to Grappling Style and Dexterity 3 grants access to Martial Arts and Defensive Combat Style. This also influences what dicepools your character is better at.<br /> <br /> The skills presented focus on meeting the minimums for merits and traits we might want to take later. I deliberately left out a lot of dots to give leeway to a large variety of concepts. These are skills for an unarmed combatant. I generally proffer unarmed to other forms of combat, but Brawl can be swapped out with Weaponry or Firearms just as easily. Depending on your Atavisms and playstyle, Athletics, Occult, and/or Expression may also replace Brawl. Always have as many dots in your skill that grants Defense as your concept will allow.<br /> <br /> Iron Skin is hands down the best merit to take if you are concerned about combat. Combat Defense keeps your defense up, but is ultimately skipable if you are willing to boost Athletics for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Unbreakable is my go-to starting atavism because it's hard to pass up immunity to several tilts and passive 3/2 armor (+1/1 on Low Saity, combine with Reinforced Clothing for another +1/0 armor) for purposes of defense. It elevates your combat beast beyond the realm of mere mortals and it just <i>feels</i> awesome and empowering to shrug off blows like that.<br /> <br /> Behold My True Form is a stopgap measure. It ensures you almost always have a source of damage (say, vs targets that can turn into swarms or turn into mist or whatever) and it helps against targets with extremely high defense. This also combines very well with Fist of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> It's important at this moment to take a look at the build's strengths and weaknesses. It is <i>very</i> defensively slanted. In terms of offense you are only inflicting 0B or 0L damage, compensated for slightly by having access to grappling. Your attack dicepools are terrible, clocking in at a mere 7 (8 during a grapple) to attack, the Defense any serious combatant is going to reduce your dicepool to somewhere between 0 and 2. This means that with the optional choices available to this build, we are going to want to address a lack of damage and a lack of reliability. It's also worth noting that while you have an &quot;okay&quot; Grapple dicepool, it isn't amazing enough to win grapple checks against other types of supernaturals who specialize.<br /> <br /> Your other choice of Atavism should probably be made around now, and you'll want something offensive. Relentless pursuit is amazing and you would be well served to pick it up as your first Experience buy, but right now what you need is more offense. I'm going to recommend the following as first-order optimal for each family:<br /> <br /> <i>Anakim: Looming Presence, Intimidate 3+ (with relevant specialty, ideally)</i><br /> This takes care of your damage issue. The low Satiety effect means that onany successful attack, you have a big chance to inflict Beaten Down. After doing that, you just need to wait out their willpower. Don't bother with Killing Instinct if you plan on relying on this.<br /> <br /> <i>Eshmaki: From the Shadows or Dragonfire; Dexterity 3; Stealth 3+ or Athletics 3+, respectively</i><br /> The advantage of Dragonfire is that it gives you a ranged (potentially multi-targeting) option that runs off of Athletics, potentially saving you the need for the defensive combat merit. Agg damage is a nice touch, but pretty situational. The real winner with Dragonfire is that it lets you use the fire Lair trait at its maximum value with impunity.<br /> <br /> From the Shadows takes a different rout. You rely on stealth (adding that dynamic to the character) and surprise attacks to negate defense. I would consider using a weapon and/or firearms with From the Shadows to perform hit and run tactics. The idea is high sudden damage, ideally enough to stun the target.<br /> <br /> <i>Makara: Monster from the Deep or Siren's Song; Expression 3+ and more Presence/Manipulation if you use Siren's Song</i><br /> Monster from the Deep is the real winner here. Not only does it lower the target's defense, but it can increase your unarmed damage and grant you an aoe attack that ignores defense entirely. This is probably the most straightforward option for those who want to be the best unarmed combatant.<br /> <br /> Siren's Song is a worthy mention. If it could harm people after making them deaf, it'd be amazing. At the moment it's a combat opener, though a pretty good one because it ignores all forms of defenses. It's more for a social / fighting hybrid, though. If you use Siren's Song I wouldn't bother with Killer Instinct.<br /> <br /> <i>Namtaru: Infestation with Fist of Nightmares and/ or Killer Instinct; Basilisk's Touch with 3 Dexterity</i><br /> It's worth noting that since Unbreakable is a Namtaru Atavism, they can use any of the other family's starting options freely.<br /> <br /> Infestation is fantastic against mortals with a Satiety expenditure. However, it simply deals too little damage by itself to be able to rely on it by itself. It's too easy to negate 1 Bashing or 1 Lethal entirely. The defenses, while great, are too situational to replace Unbreakable entirely. The answer to these problems are Fist of Nightmares and Killer Instinct 3 + Killer Instinct (Advanced) 1. The former lets you apply damage or other effects to your swarm cloud, while the latter lets you ignore armor and convert your AoE 1 Bashing damage to an AoE 1 Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Basilisk's Touch is probably on par with Monster from the Deep. In some ways it's better. A simple touch (Dexterity + Brawl +2, helping your dicepools) can inflict poison and/or the drugged tilt. Combine poison with inflicting Insensate and the fight is over, the opponent just doesn't know it yet.<br /> <br /> <i>Ugallu: Storm Lashed + Occult 3+ or Eye of Heaven</i><br /> Storm Lashed offers a variety of special effects and a special means of attack, all of which are useful. Nabbing a second point of Lair so that you can blind someone for multiple turns becomes important, though probably not enough to bother starting with it. Make sure to boost your lightning dicepool if you plan on relying on that. <br /> <br /> Eye of Heaven is situational and requires you to be the one taking initaitive, but is pretty nice. Note that its Satiety effect can apply to things like Nightmares or anything else classified as an &quot;attack.&quot; Personally I think there are better options, but Eye of Heaven offers enough utility to be worth considering.<br /> <br /> <i>On Cyclopian Strength, Limb from Limb, etc.</i><br /> Things that deal damage based on Lair are pretty good, but IMO not worth starting out with. Limb from Limb is a great Atavism, but this build suffers from a lack of damage, and you need damage to make Limb from Limb work properly.<br /> <br /> <i>Summary</i><br /> Looming Presence, Monster from the Deep, and Basilisk's Touch are probably the best option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T18:04:30-07:00","id":644805,"title":"","content":"Just remember that Combat by Rote negates Defense and precludes making Called Shots or taking other focused combat actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T18:36:33-07:00","id":644817,"title":"","content":"Where is that rule, anyways? I've only actually used it during a grapple, where the loss of defense and etc. don't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T22:10:51-07:00","id":644921,"title":"","content":"Well that's certainly a thorough explanation SoulGambit. Nice work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T22:17:00-07:00","id":644922,"title":"","content":"In the original printing of Professional Training, in Hunter: the Vigil, there was a Sidebar explaining how Applying the Rote quality to Combat Actions worked and what that represented in real world terms, and what the appropriate drawbacks were to doing so, namely that all of your focus is on acting in accordance with your training rather than on reacting to external threats and the realities of a combat situation. I'll double check Demon and the GMC, but I believe that that's still a balancing effort on the part of the dev team.<br /> <br /> UPDATE: neither of the newer books include the <i>Combat by Rote</i> sidebar (Hunter: the Vigil, pp. 69) with their versions of Professional Training, however not imposing the loss of Defense limitation would make the merit as a whole an auto-take for the vast majority of combat builds, as it would make the All-out Attack option, and abilities that utilize the similar mechanics, redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 08-30-2015, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T08:54:07-07:00","id":645445,"title":"","content":"No comment on Birthrights in combat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T10:15:15-07:00","id":645546,"title":"","content":"&quot;Can't hide from me, mofo.&quot;<br /> <br /> So in all seriousness, why are we only concerned with combat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T12:08:25-07:00","id":645654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=645546#post645546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Can't hide from me, mofo.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So in all seriousness, why are we only concerned with combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's the question that the OP asked about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T14:02:23-07:00","id":645866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/641688-power-level-of-beasts?p=645445#post645445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No comment on Birthrights in combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anakim's is a little too situational, but the others work brilliantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 08-30-2015, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T17:01:04-07:00","id":646102,"title":"","content":"I can't support using sidebars in 1e splatbooks people may or may not have as a default assumption for how rules 2e Corebooks, which are meant to stand alone, work. That said, it's certainly a fine houserule. Professional training always gets a &quot;talk to your ST first&quot; from me because of how powerful Rote in combat is. However, in the case of mortals and beast, it's not that huge of a deal. It matters for Vampires and Werewolves because they can get rather huge dicepools. Beasts bizzarly lack dice adders, but pack a huge punch when they do hit.<br /> <br /> With Birthrights, &quot;use them as much as you can&quot;? They are often free, after all. I'm not sure what discussion can really be had about them. I certinly wouldn't pick a family just because of how its birthright impacts combat. I will say I consider Ugallu to be the overall best birthright, but that's more because I like spotting hidden enemies than because it's actually the best.<br /> <br /> @ArcaneArts: S'what the OP asked, mostly. Mono-focusing on combat is a fool's gambit, I admit. I tried to leave enough room even in the combat builds for well-rounded characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T17:30:44-07:00","id":646133,"title":"","content":"Missed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}